Chromium 159.0.8154.18 -> 159.0.8154.28, for the 159.0.8154.18 tarball.

159.0.8154.28 is a tag on the 159 branch (refs/branch-heads/8154@{#1026}) that
has no source tarball (as of 2026-11-19: Google's lite bucket's newest 159 is .18,
chromium-linux-tarballs' is .13). It adds 155 branch commits to
159.0.8154.18 (#871), the newest tag with a tarball, among them PGO/orderfile
rolls, translation updates and VERSION increments. It adds, among many CHECKs
turned back into DCHECKs and Omnibox (the location bar's dropdown on the
Unbounded Element API), Contextual Tasks, NTP Aurora V2 and aim-drive changes:
WebCodecs' callbacks routed to the execution context's task runners,
SyncLoadContext's completion deferred while handling redirects, ServiceWorker's
fetch response callbacks invoked directly from Take(), its startup queued during
network restriction registration and its last committed client updated only on
navigation commit, File System Access' platform path resolution disallowed in
incognito, OTP's PSL matching in non-login flows behind a flag, a dangling Asset
reference in WindowFrameProviderGtk, a TopLayerElements mutation while iterating
in DisplayLockContext; in the dependency rolls: ANGLE's translator validating
gl_PerVertex member types and its GL back-end reading pixels via a scratch FBO
for MRT, Skia's Ganesh image filtering mipmap fix, V8 15.9.128.12 to .16 (among
them JitAllocationType in StartOfAllocationAt, the JSDispatchEntry parameter
count race, MapRef's instance_type TOCTOU) and Dawn's DawnWireServices lock.

Generated from the upstream diffs between the tags: chromium/src
refs/tags/159.0.8154.18..refs/tags/159.0.8154.28 and the dependencies whose
DEPS revision changed (ANGLE 0f0b90f0b5bf..b49535777c51, Skia
8a65fa27c104..458e1f1ab81e, V8 4593f4dc1e9b..ff20afeabcd5, Dawn
69bfa246b5d7..16b69da1f131: no file of Dawn's is kept, only the stamps below
change), as served by Gitiles, with scripts/chromium-delta. The other
dependencies' DEPS revisions don't change (the .18 tarball has them).

Left out, as they cannot affect a Linux build: files not in the release
tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
translations (but en-GB), CI configuration, PGO/orderfile pointers, submodule
pointer updates, DEPS. GN files (*.gn, *.gni) are kept even for tests and other
platforms: gn gen reads test targets' BUILD.gn too.

Added: the tarball's stamp files for the new commit (stamps.py:
build/util/LASTCHANGE{,.committime}, gpu/config/gpu_lists_version.h,
skia/ext/skia_commit_hash.h, gpu/webgpu/DAWN_VERSION and
gpu/webgpu/dawn_commit_hash.h; commit
6667d1ef5cc7735c59c67adf7e03ccbc07f499e7, refs/branch-heads/8154@{#1026}).
build/util/MINIBRANCH doesn't change.

Checked: applies to the 159.0.8154.18 tarball; chrome/VERSION becomes
159.0.8154.28; every patched source file is byte-identical to its version
at the tag (or its dependency's DEPS revision); it adds 2 files and deletes
none; the 159.0.8154.18 tarball's non-git files are all classified
(tarball-generated.py with generated.conf).

Apply with git apply.

